<main><a href="/">← Back to application</a><h1>API documentation</h1><p>One SvelteKit Node server serves these same-origin endpoints. This page documents the API; it does not submit paid model requests.</p><a href="/openapi.json">Download OpenAPI 3.1</a>
<article class="lesson-step"><h2>GET /api/health</h2><p>Returns connectivity and whether a server key is configured. It does not test authentication or billing.</p><CodeBlock language="json" code={'{"status":"ok","api_key_configured":false}'} /></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h2>POST /api/agent/query</h2><p>Send application/json with a trimmed prompt of 1–4000 characters. Returns answer, turns, duration_ms, total_cost_usd and is_error.</p><CodeBlock language="json" code={'{"prompt":"Hello world!"}'} /></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h2>POST /api/agent/stream</h2><p>Same JSON body. Returns UTF-8 SSE message events containing safe SDK projections, then done. A failure sends error and closes without done. This is SDK message streaming, rather than individual tokens. Comments are heartbeats.</p><CodeBlock language="text" code={'event: error\ndata: {"detail":"Configure ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the project .env before running the agent."}\n\n'} /></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h2>Validation and errors</h2><p>400 malformed JSON · 403 foreign origin · 413 body above 32 KiB · 415 wrong content type · 422 invalid prompt · 503 missing key in query mode · 502 provider failure in query mode. After SSE headers, errors use the error event. SDK error results retain is_error even if transport completes. Execution has a three-minute deadline and disconnect cancellation.</p></article></main>
